The size calculation for `scontrol->size` correctly includes `sizeof(struct sof_ipc4_control_data)`, but the allocation uses `scontrol->max_size` as the total size. However, `max_size` only represents the payload (sizeof(sof_abi_hdr) + actual payload), omitting the kernel-only `sizeof(struct sof_ipc4_control_data)`. This results in insufficient memory allocation. Additionally, the validation check incorrectly treats `max_size` as if it includes `sizeof(*control_data)`, allowing undersized allocations that lead to out-of-bounds writes when accessing `control_data->data`.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
