scontrol->ipc_control_data = kzalloc(sizeof(*control_data) + scontrol->max_size, GFP_KERNEL);
if (scontrol->max_size < sizeof(struct sof_abi_hdr)) {
if (scontrol->priv_size > scontrol->max_size) {
```
Reason:
The allocation now correctly adds `sizeof(*control_data)` to `scontrol->max_size`, ensuring enough memory for both the kernel-only control data structure and the full payload (sof_abi_hdr + payload). The validation checks are corrected to treat `max_size` as purely the payload size (must be at least `sizeof(struct sof_abi_hdr)`) and to compare `priv_size` directly against `max_size` without subtracting `sizeof(*control_data)`. This prevents both undersized and oversized initial data, guaranteeing safe memory usage.

